'.\" -*- nroff -*-
.TH KAFS-V7 8 "2026-07-16" "kafs 0.4.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
kafs-v7 \- dedicated format v7 runtime entrypoint
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kafs-v7
.RB --image
.I image
.B --inspection-mount
.I mountpoint
.BR -o " " ro
.RI [ FUSE\ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kafs-v7
is the dedicated format v7 runtime entrypoint.
It validates the format v7 CLI boundary, rejects legacy
.B v6_*
mount-option mode tokens, runs descriptor/checkpoint preflight, and admits an
accepted format v7 image for read-only inspection.
.PP
Inspection admission is limited to a selected descriptor/checkpoint pair at
.B checkpoint_seq=0
with empty journal segments.  A single surviving valid recovery pair may be
mounted in degraded inspection mode.  Divergent or unpaired state fails closed
before FUSE starts.
.PP
The backing image is opened read-only, mapped read-only, and mounted with FUSE
.BR ro .
Mutation requests fail with
.BR EROFS ,
and the selected checkpoint's recovered free-block and free-inode counters are
reported by
.BR statfs (2).
.PP
Format v6 was an experimental implementation used to split the runtime
entrypoint, descriptor admission, and controlled-write policy away from the
production
.BR kafs (1)
binary.  Format v7 is the breaking-change continuation of that work.  The
current v7 implementation has its own entrypoint, admission, selected runtime
view, layout, and adapter source set and does not route successful admission
through the v6 public wire/layout entrypoint.
.PP
The existing
.B kafs
binary remains the v4/v5 production runtime entrypoint and fails closed for
format v6/v7 images.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -h ", " --help
Show help and exit.
.TP
.BR --image " " <image>
Specify the format v7 image path.
.TP
.BR --image= "<image>"
Specify the format v7 image path using the inline form.
.TP
.B --inspection-mount
Select the read-only v7 inspection contract.
The request must include
.BR -o " " ro .
.TP
.B --controlled-write-mount
Reserved for a future v7 controlled-write contract.  The option is recognized,
but current runtime admission fails closed and does not modify the image.
.TP
.BR --option " " <opt[,opt...]>
Alias for FUSE
.BR -o .
.TP
.BR --option= "<opt[,opt...]>"
Inline form of
.BR --option .
.SH CURRENT LIMITS
Non-empty journal replay, repair, controlled write, checkpoint publication,
multi-group mutation, cross-group HRL mutation, migration, and hotplug write
delegation are not enabled by this entrypoint.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Help was printed.
.TP
.B 2
The request was invalid, the image was not format v7, descriptor preflight
failed, or runtime admission failed.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kafs (1),
.BR kafs-v6 (8),
.BR mkfs.kafs (8),
.BR fsck.kafs (8),
.BR kafsdump (8)
.SH AUTHOR
kafs project.
